===Noun===
{{en-noun}} {{term-label|en|medicine}}

# A [[person#Noun|person]] or an [[animal#Noun|animal]] that [[exhibit#Verb|exhibits]] no [[symptom]]s of [[disease#Noun|disease]].
#: {{ant|en|symptomatic#Noun}}
#: {{ux|en|After a 10-day observation period, group 1 was divided into subgroup 1A (symptomatics) and subgroup 1B ('''asymptomatics''').}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Rachel Jenkins [''et al.'']|title=Prevalence of Malaria Parasites in Adults and Its Determinants in Malaria Endemic Area of Kisumu County, Kenya|journal=w:Malaria Journal|location=London|publisher=w:BioMed Central|date=8 July 2015|doi=10.1186/s12936-015-0781-5|volume=14|section=article 263|page=5|column=2|issn=1475-2875|oclc=891213153|passage=[S]uch a high adult prevalence of parasites emphasises the relevance of the adult malaria parasite reservoir on the transmission of disease in both children and adults and it supports the need for further consideration and research evaluation of treatment of '''asymptomatics''', including approaches such as intermittent screening and treatment (IST) as part of an integrated malaria control programme, if malaria elimination is to be achieved.}}
# ''Preceded by'' '''[[the#Article|the]]''': people or animals that exhibit no symptoms of disease regarded [[collectively]].
#: {{ux|en|At the end of the observation period, those who are still symptomatic require second-line treatment, whereas '''the asymptomatic''' are discharged.}}

